```

## How litellm is involved

Litellm is not currently mapping the tool indexes. It currently assigns the tools the index of their chunk, and instead it needs to assign the tools based on their own index, not based on the chunk index. For example see here https://github.com/BerriAI/litellm/blob/main/litellm/llms/anthropic.py#L1190

Handle bedrock tool calling in stream_chunk_builder
              @krrishdholakia Sure, here you go!

```python
import litellm

model = "claude-3-5-sonnet-20240620"

system_prompt = """
You're a chatbot that answers data questions using SQL.
You have a `sql_query` tool to help you get at the data you need.
Make sure to explain to the user how you're coming up with the answer,
including the SQL.
"""

messages = [
    {"role": "system", "content": system_prompt},
    {"role": "user", "content": "How many rows are there in the 'users' table?"},
]

tools = [
    {
        "type": "function",
        "function": {
            "name": "sql_query",
            "parameters": {
                "type": "object",
                "properties": {
                    "query": {
                        "type": "string",
                        "description": "A valid SQL query in PostgresQL format",
                    }
                },
                "required": ["query"],
            },
        },
    }
]


response = litellm.completion(model, messages, tools=tools, stream=True)
chunks = list(response)
print(chunks)

result = litellm.stream_chunk_builder(chunks)
assert result.choices[0].message.tool_calls is not None
```

