Handle bedrock tool calling in stream_chunk_builder
## Title

Handle bedrock tool calling in stream_chunk_builder

## Relevant issues

Fixes #5022

## Type

🐛 Bug Fix

## Changes

The streaming chunks from Anthropic seem to violate an assumption that is implicit in the stream_chunk_builder implementation: that only tool_calls OR function_calls OR content will appear in a streamed response. The repro in #5022 shows that you can get content followed by tool calls.

These changes properly handle these combinations by building separate lists of each type of chunk (note that in theory a chunk could appear in multiple lists, e.g. both delta.tool_calls and delta.content being present on one chunk).

## [REQUIRED] Testing

```python
import dotenv
import litellm

dotenv.load_dotenv()

model = "claude-3-5-sonnet-20240620"

system_prompt = """
You're a chatbot that answers data questions using SQL.
You have a `sql_query` tool to help you get at the data you need.
Make sure to explain to the user how you're coming up with the answer,
including the SQL.
"""

messages = [
    {"role": "system", "content": system_prompt},
    {"role": "user", "content": "How many rows are there in the 'users' table?"},
]

tools = [
    {
        "type": "function",
        "function": {
            "name": "sql_query",
            "parameters": {
                "type": "object",
                "properties": {
                    "query": {
                        "type": "string",
                        "description": "A valid SQL query in PostgresQL format",
                    }
                },
                "required": ["query"],
            },
        },
    }
]


response = litellm.completion(model, messages, tools=tools, stream=True)
chunks = list(response)

result = litellm.stream_chunk_builder(chunks)
assert result.choices[0].message.tool_calls is not None
print(result.to_json())
```
